WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.000
Every year, millions of American homes lose power — sometimes for days.

00:07.000 --> 00:15.000
A home standby generator watches your power around the clock — and takes over automatically.

00:15.000 --> 00:23.000
When the grid fails, the transfer switch senses it and moves your home to generator power in about ten seconds.

00:23.000 --> 00:31.000
Heat stays on. Food stays cold. Medical devices, Wi-Fi, work-from-home — uninterrupted.

00:31.000 --> 00:38.000
It runs on your natural gas line — or a propane tank sized for your longest outage.

00:38.000 --> 00:46.000
A yearly service visit and a weekly self-test keep it ready. Most failures are just skipped maintenance.

00:46.000 --> 00:54.000
Correct placement plus working CO detectors on every level. Safety first — always.

00:54.000 --> 00:58.000
HomeGeneratorGuide.com — independent guides for US homeowners.
